From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:58:04 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] viz: BeginFrames from the display's vertical blank on Windows
 10 Mobile

Without DirectComposition, Windows gets BeginFrames from a timer whose
phase and interval are steered from outside. On a phone that timer sits on
the system's interrupt grid (8 ms on battery), and nothing can keep it in
step with a panel that refreshes every 16.98 ms.

ExternalBeginFrameSourceW10m ticks from a thread that waits in
IDXGIOutput::WaitForVBlank, as gecko-w10m does: one pending tick at most,
tick times on a steady grid one measured interval apart, asleep while
nobody wants frames, a timer's ticks while the display is off or the wait
hangs. Every ten seconds of animation the log says how the ticks went.
--vw-vsync=timer keeps the timer. And the output surface does not write
vsync parameters of its own over what is measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
